WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.360
TrustRail MENA checks network evidence before money moves. This

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.825
is a working remittance wallet prototype, using live Nokia

00:00:07.885 --> 00:00:13.235
simulator calls, synthetic customers, and a clearly synthetic voice.

00:00:14.285 --> 00:00:17.290
Aisha is sending five thousand dirhams from Dubai to

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.460
a first time beneficiary in Pakistan. She confirms in

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.565
the wallet. Its backend asks TrustRail for a recommendation.

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:31.075
LangGraph coordinates Gemini planning, network checks, and institution owned

00:00:31.135 --> 00:00:35.655
policy. The wallet controls the payment. No real money

00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:36.825
moves.

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:42.969
The suspicious transfer returns HOLD. SIM Swap and Device

00:00:43.029 --> 00:00:47.574
Swap report recent changes. Location and roaming provide additional

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:52.059
context. These signals justify review, not a claim of

00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:56.169
proven fraud. The trace shows the actual model, API

00:00:56.229 --> 00:01:00.794
evidence, and timing. The model cannot override policy.

00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:05.317
A routine family transfer returns APPROVE with the two

00:01:05.377 --> 00:01:09.117
required checks. This means the wallet may continue under

00:01:09.177 --> 00:01:13.267
its own rules. TrustRail does not authorize or execute

00:01:13.327 --> 00:01:14.497
the payment.

00:01:15.547 --> 00:01:18.072
Now keep the payment identical and change only the

00:01:18.132 --> 00:01:21.617
note. The customer is visiting her sister in Muscat

00:01:21.677 --> 00:01:24.942
and using her mobile there. We run again.

00:01:31.672 --> 00:01:35.387
Gemini adds a Roaming Status check. This is context

00:01:35.447 --> 00:01:40.367
sensitive tool selection, not three fixed presets. Travel alone

00:01:40.427 --> 00:01:42.372
is not treated as fraud.

00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:46.727
What if a network signal is missing? The simulator

00:01:46.787 --> 00:01:52.497
intentionally makes Device Swap unavailable. TrustRail returns VERIFY, directing

00:01:52.557 --> 00:01:54.352
the wallet to stronger verification.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:59.972
It never substitutes invented safe evidence. Attempts are bounded,

00:02:00.032 --> 00:02:02.647
inside a seven second server budget.

00:02:03.697 --> 00:02:07.062
Our first buyer is a remittance wallet. The proposed

00:02:07.122 --> 00:02:10.377
model is usage based pricing, with a pilot measuring

00:02:10.437 --> 00:02:15.657
false holds, verification completion, latency, and cost per decision.

00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:19.502
Real deployment still needs confirmed carrier coverage, consent, and

00:02:19.562 --> 00:02:24.392
local data processing. These are pilot requirements, not results

00:02:24.452 --> 00:02:30.947
already achieved. AI proposes checks. Policy decides. The wallet

00:02:31.007 --> 00:02:32.727
stays in control.
